 "path": "arc-notes/task-b563b005.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC pattern note: task-b563b005\n\nObserved rule from demo and solved test: a grid is partitioned by a solid-color line (in the demo, vertical and horizontal 1-lines; in test, 2-lines). Treat each corresponding compartment as a tiled/duplicated cell pattern. Copy the populated pattern into the blank counterpart compartment(s) with the same orientation and relative cell coordinates; do not rotate or reflect. Repeated compartment blocks along an axis use the same template. In the test, columns 0–1 and 3–4 correspond across the vertical divider at column 2; the populated rows 8–14 in the right compartment provided the template repeated in rows 0–6 and 16–22, while the horizontal divider rows remained intact. The demo similarly showed the populated upper-right quadrant copied to the upper-left and lower quadrants. Useful cue: odd-color cells are sparse pattern marks, while full monochrome rows/columns are separators."
}
